  "comment": "What the map generator (D50) places, per game family: monsters by tier (1 weak .. 4 tough; boss = only in the boss arena), with the engine's own editor numbers, health and radius (a test holds them to the engine's catalogue); weapons in the order a map hands them out, the ammunition each uses and the damage a unit of it does on average (Doom's as the Balance meter counts them); health, armour, keys (colour, object, the lock a door takes) and the decorations dressed into rooms. 'doom2' marks what only the Doom II family has. 'start' is the damage the ammunition a player starts with can do. 'lights' and 'torches' are the decorations that give light (lamps for tech rooms; torches for castles and caves), placed where a room's light comes from. 'powerups' are the game's own by what they are for: strength (berserk), pack (backpack), boost (megasphere), suit (against hurting floors), map, hide, shield (invulnerability), sight; 'doom2Powerups' are those only the Doom II family has.",
